13583	{"artifactId":"LLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s1","entry":{"id":"review-b6cf4c0e54e2479c4f4dea04c29bc765","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:56:43.504Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's §7 acceptance-mapping table maps at least one test subject to every one of Story s1's own six acceptance criteria (ac1-ac6) from DEF.md.","evidence":"DEF.md lines 79-84 define s1's ac1 through ac6 (operationalizing k1-k8). LLD §7's 'Acceptance mapping' table has a row for ac1, ac2, ac3, ac4, ac5 and ac6, each citing concrete test subjects (e.g. ac1 -> 'packet scope ... no final/head commit', ac4 -> 'per-task checkpoint atomicity', '5/10/15-minute task deadline with continuation'). [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/DEF.md, docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none — upstream intent is covered","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD does not design the non-goal work explicitly reserved to s2 (resume/re-review) or s3 (session/concurrency/cleanup integration) — it only names those boundaries, it does not implement them.","evidence":"HLD.md §6.2/§6.3 assign recovery/re-review policy to s2 and session-integration/concurrency/cleanup to s3; HLD §8 Rollout Phase A lists only Story 's1'. The LLD's §1 'Adjacent scope' section reproduces that boundary verbatim and §2/§3 (contracts, data model) define only sc1-sc3 types owned by s1 (ReviewPacket, ReviewCheckpoint, TaskReviewResult, TaskBasedCodeReviewBody) with no attempt-resume selection logic or worker/cleanup logic designed. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/HLD.md, docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`handleCodeReviewStep` currently has the signature `(input: unknown, deps: CodeReviewStepDeps = DEFAULT_DEPS): Promise<CodeReviewStepMcpEnvelope>` as the LLD §2.1 states.","evidence":"src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts:215-218 reads `export async function handleCodeReviewStep(input: unknown, deps: CodeReviewStepDeps = DEFAULT_DEPS): Promise<CodeReviewStepMcpEnvelope>`, matching the LLD's `handleCodeReviewStep(input: unknown, deps?: CodeReviewStepDeps): Promise<CodeReviewStepMcpEnvelope>`. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`runReviewSession` today is a single-attempt, non-retried, deadline-bound read-only CLI session that throws `ReviewSessionTimeoutError` when the deadline passes, as LLD §2.2 claims.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:456-491: `internalRetry false: the caller re-issues, so this call makes one attempt only`; `if (remainingMs <= 0) throw new ReviewSessionTimeoutError(opts.deadlineMs)`; comment confirms it is the read-only sibling of runEditSession used by design review. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ReviewPacket, ReviewCommit, ChangedSegment, TaskReviewResult, TaskReviewAssignment, ReviewCheckpoint and TaskBasedCodeReviewBody, all labelled 'new' in LLD §3, do not already exist anywhere in src/.","evidence":"A repo-wide grep for these identifier names across src/ returned zero matches in any non-artifact, non-doc TypeScript file (only the LLD's own artifact JSON and the HLD/LLD docs reference them), confirming these types are genuinely new, not pre-existing under another name. [files: src]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`roundWriterFor`, which LLD §2.3 claims to reuse rather than invent, already exists with the stated shape and is already consumed by the code-review handler/controller and build-step phases.","evidence":"src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:74 defines `export function roundWriterFor(repoPath: string, actor: Actor = BUILD_ACTOR): RoundWriter`; it is imported and called in handler.ts, controller.ts, code-review-rpc.ts and build-step/phases/implement.ts and validate.ts, matching the LLD's 'reuse the existing canonical artifact queue/round-write seam' claim. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites listed for `roundWriterFor`/`ReviewPacket` integration (`src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts`, `src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts`) are real files that already import and call `roundWriterFor` today, grounding the LLD's claimed integration point.","evidence":"handler.ts:49 `import { roundWriterFor } from '../../lifecycle-registry.js'` and line 513 `(deps.roundWriterFor ?? roundWriterFor)(payload.subject.repoPath)`; code-review-rpc.ts:28 and :138 do the same. Both files exist and are exactly where the LLD says the new packet-driven path must plug in. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The legacy `validateArtifact` / CR writer (cited c7/c12) is correctly described as enforcing exact dimension order/count and re-folding verdict from counts, which is why task-based results cannot pass through it unchanged — this is the real change-site risk the LLD must route around with a separate version-2 validator.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts:364-389: `validateArtifact` checks `b.dimensions.length !== expectedDims.length`, each `dimensions[i].dimension` against `expectedDims[i]` in order, and re-folds `foldCounts`/`foldVerdict` against `b.counts`/`b.verdict` — exactly the 'exact dimension membership/order and folds counts/verdict' behavior the LLD's c7/c12 citations and §2.3 postcondition describe. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every CR record already carries a `schemaVersion` field (currently always 1), so adding a `schemaVersion: 2` task-based body alongside unchanged version-1 records, as the LLD's §3.4/§8 migration proposes, is structurally compatible with the current artifact shape.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts:333 stamps `schemaVersion: CODE_REVIEW_SCHEMA_VERSION` (= 1, defined in types.ts:280) into every written CR record's meta — the exact field the LLD's version-aware reader/writer design would branch on. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No code today writes or reads a `TaskBasedCodeReviewBody` / `schemaVersion: 2` record; the per-task checkpoint and version-2 CR are genuinely unimplemented, matching the LLD's own 'State before' migration claim.","evidence":"Grep across src/ for TaskBasedCodeReviewBody/ReviewCheckpoint returned no matches outside the LLD's own artifact files and docs, and the LLD §8 'State before' explicitly states 'The proposed selected-change packet and per-task checkpoint are new, not already implemented' — consistent with what the repo shows. [files: src]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'Adjacent scope' prose for s2 and s3 is a verbatim restatement of HLD §6.2/§6.3 story-boundary ownership, and the LLD's contracts/data model only implement sc1-sc3 functionality assigned to s1, not s2/s3 behavior.","evidence":"HLD.md §6.2 ('Own interrupted-attempt continuation and history-aware re-review policy...') and §6.3 ('Own normal entrypoint/session integration and concurrency/approval cleanup verification...') are reproduced character-for-character in LLD §1 'Adjacent scope (owned by other stories — do NOT implement here)'. LLD §2/§3 contain no resume-selection, worker-lifecycle or cleanup-on-approval implementation. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/HLD.md, docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"HLD §6.1 and §8 assign sc1-sc3 and Rollout Phase A to Story s1 alone, matching the LLD's own 'Owns: sc1, sc2, sc3' / 'Rollout phase: A' framing — the LLD is not redesigning a shared contract owned by another story.","evidence":"HLD.md §6.1 'Story STORY-...-s1 — Owns: sc1, sc2, sc3'; §8 Rollout 'A — useful scoped review — Stories: s1'. LLD §1 HLD context states 'Rollout phase: A' and 'Owns: sc1 ..., sc2 ..., sc3 ...' identically. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'Invalid or unresolved submitted scope' error case implements DEF.md ac1's requirement that missing/inconsistent scope fail explicitly without a HEAD-based fallback.","evidence":"DEF.md:79 ac1: 'missing or inconsistent scope fails explicitly without a HEAD-based fallback or redundant dependency input'. LLD §6 first error case: 'Return invalid-packet before model execution or checkpoint acknowledgement; identify the offending entry without substituting a HEAD diff.' The detection/response/impact triad traces directly to the real upstream criterion. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/DEF.md, docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's S/M/L task-deadline error case (5/10/15 minutes -> incomplete on timeout, failed on provider/malformed error, remaining tasks continue) matches DEF ac4 and HLD §7's non-functional target.","evidence":"DEF.md:82 ac4: 'S/M/L limits are 5/10/15 minutes, timeout records incomplete and review continues'. HLD.md §7 Performance: 'S/M/L task execution ceilings are 5/10/15 minutes ... timeout produces incomplete and continues'. LLD §3.3 TaskReviewAssignment.timeoutMs: 300000|600000|900000 and §6 'Task deadline or provider failure' case reproduce this exactly. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/DEF.md, docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every one of Story s1's own six acceptance criteria (ac1-ac6) is mapped to at least one named test subject in the LLD's §7 acceptance-mapping table.","evidence":"LLD §7 'Acceptance mapping' table lists rows for ac1 through ac6 inclusive, each with one or more concrete proving test subjects drawn from the unit/contract/integration/live levels described just above it. [files: docs/epics/review-committed-work-task-checkpoints-E20261030e6ddcdcb/S001/LLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's claimed test framework ('Existing Node node:test/assert TypeScript *.test.ts patterns') matches the real existing code-review test suite it says to follow.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/runner.test.ts:6-9 imports `{ test } from 'node:test'` and `assert from 'node:assert/strict'`, confirming the convention cited in LLD reference [[c9]] and §7's 'Test framework' line is accurate to the real repo. [files: src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/runner.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T19:56:43.504Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
